  "title": "SideKick wrong on C0 GPIO in STANDBY",
  "content": "<p>  </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/68017c71-1079-478c-ab42-f4fccc5f348f.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>But C0 does have the option to configure pull-up/down in STANDBY:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/fb099a5e-d207-4bcd-9759-307a070de333.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>Note also that it references the wrong RM:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/483d1a5d-dc75-499a-b8a5-acb88a04db87.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p> </p><p>When asking the question more generally, Sidekick does note the pull-up/down option for other families - but does not include C0:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/6e87ea64-27fb-4a22-a4ee-a7d06dadf784.png\" /></figure><p> </p>",
